``` CL-02 | Which Peer Dropped During a Network Partition
    Splunk Administrator Field Manual - Gaurav Malik

    Use case: Identify which peer node dropped out of the cluster during a
    network partition, and the exact second the cluster manager marked it
    Down.
    Run on: SH for the transition history, CM for live heartbeat state.
    Query: Live heartbeat age (CM)
```
| rest splunk_server=local /services/cluster/master/peers
| eval hb_age_s=now()-last_heartbeat
| table label site status is_searchable hb_age_s bucket_count host_port_pair
| sort - hb_age_s
